  "conclusions": {
    "publication": "Context/ingress generation/armed boundary are retained across pop and FPU work, then checked at locked publication. Races discard/restart the separate Capture series; a held old valid sample cannot satisfy current context.",
    "command_lifetime": "Each admitted internal command retains immutable original sample time/deadline and Capture fault generation. New good publications preserve old deadlines. Invalid/failed publication advances a permanent publication floor; earlier commands cannot revive after same-generation recovery. Rejected current publication is not reported current. Both fuel and spark must be cut to bypass required flex qualification.",
    "ACK": "Only the serialized control owner bridges exact offered port publication/context/generation and observed Capture fault/config epoch after a completed invalid evaluation. Diagnostic reads, stale tickets, mutex misses and skipped control do not ACK. New ISR/configuration faults invalidate old consumption.",
    "restart": "Restart clears waveform/filter/gap continuity, preserves monotonic input/query/source/fault history, and requires a new complete coherent window. Long intentional stop does not create stale/gap refaults, but backwards input/owner/query time still fails closed.",
    "time_mapping": "Flex alone uses a fixed conservative pre-sync epoch and floor tick conversion. Native counter/phase/bracket/wrap/latency models preserve1/3/5ms widths; old crank mapper behavior remains identical. No shared capture timer resync is introduced.",
    "target_source": "Only the serialized monitor/control task owns FPU Capture. Configuration/request calibration and tune/sensor revisions are immutable producer context; required acquisition includes corrections-Off ETH dependencies. Synthetic sources and unconfirmed/unavailable/mismatched contexts cannot qualify.",
    "hardware_API_source": "Pinned local SDK first-free allocation plus the two preceding group0 channels establish flex slot2. GPIO38 is input-only in the distinct draft profile; only its capture interrupt/status bits are modified. The source ISR queues bounded integer records and never refreshes crank/cam producer age.",
    "diagnostics": "Read-only copied publications use lossless decimal U64 counters/times, expose requested versus producer identity and command floor, reject contradictory qualified tuples, and clear current wording on failed HTTP polling. Host status explicitly has no measured target capture. Deadline fixture correctly distinguishes a new qualified publication from an expired older command.",
